{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdmondsKarpEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Capacity","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each round a breadth-first search over the residual network, its rows in edge-position order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finds a shortest augmenting path from the source to the sink, stopping when the sink is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered. The path is reported with its bottleneck, the smallest residual along it; then the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bottleneck is sent along it one edge at a time, from the source end: pushed along an edge with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room to spare, or cancelled on an edge whose flow the path runs against. When the sink cannot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be reached the flow is maximum and nothing more is reported."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/EdmondsKarpEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentat